The attached image (Fig. 4 from the PDF) demonstrates the uptake of FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA, green) and AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) via confocal microscopy. The top row shows BMDCs incubated with Nano-11 only, exhibiting intracellular red fluorescence. The middle row shows BMDCs incubated with soluble OVA, showing minimal green fluorescence. The bottom row illustrates BMDCs incubated with OVA adsorbed to Nano-11, where both Nano-11 and OVA are efficiently phagocytized and colocalize within the cells (appearing yellow in the merged image). This visual evidence supports Nano-11's role in enhancing antigen delivery to dendritic cells.